---
id: granny-smith-maple-walnut-overnight-oats
title: Granny Smith, Maple & Walnut Overnight Oats
category: breakfast
meal_role: overnight_oats

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 370

storage:
  fridge_days: 2
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Cut a quarter from a @granny-smith-apples{1/4%count}, trim away the core, and coarsely grate it skin on, on a box grater, straight into a jar or bowl. Wrap the rest of the apple and refrigerate it for the next jars. Add @rolled-oats{1/3%cup}, @chia-seeds{1%tbsp}, and @ground-cinnamon{1/2%tsp}.

Stir @maple-syrup{1%tsp} into @partly-skimmed-milk-2pct{1%cup} so it sweetens the whole jar evenly, pour it in, and stir well so the chia and cinnamon don't clump. Cover and refrigerate overnight ~chill{8%hour}.

In the morning, warm in the #microwave for ~reheat{2%minute} until hot. Stir, top with @chopped-walnuts{2%tbsp}, and serve.
